---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../site.config.js';
---

<Page
  title="Disclaimer"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  lede="What this site is, and what it is not."
  updated="29 August 2026"
>
  <h2>No affiliation</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is independent. We are not affiliated with, authorised by, endorsed by or sponsored by any school,
    university, company, organization, government body or individual described on this site. Profiles are written
    without the involvement of their subjects. Names and marks belong to their owners and appear here descriptively.
  </p>

  <h2>Not an official record</h2>
  <p>
    This site is not a government register, an accreditation body, a ranking, or an official record of any entity. It
    is a compilation of what published sources say. Where an official record exists, that record — not this page — is
    authoritative, and we link to it wherever we can.
  </p>

  <h2>Not advice</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing here is legal, financial, admissions, employment, medical or investment advice. If you are choosing a
    school, evaluating an organization or making any other consequential decision, verify the underlying facts
    directly with the entity and with the relevant official body.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy and currency</h2>
  <p>
    Profiles are accurate to the sources cited, as at the last-updated date shown on each page. Institutions change
    leadership, addresses, status and accreditation, and sources are sometimes wrong or later corrected. An unverified
    claim is listed as an open item on the profile rather than presented as fact.
  </p>

  <h2>Neutrality</h2>
  <p>
    A profile existing on this site is not an endorsement, a recommendation, a rating or a judgement of quality. The
    absence of a profile means nothing at all about an entity — it usually means we have not researched it yet. We do
    not rank subjects and do not describe them as "best", "top" or "leading".
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>
    We link to external sources so readers can verify claims. We are not responsible for the content or availability
    of those sites, and a link is not an endorsement of anything else they publish.
  </p>

  <h2>Fair use of quoted material</h2>
  <p>
    Short quotations from cited sources are used for reporting, verification and comment, with attribution and a link.
    Rights in the quoted material remain with the original publisher. If you are a rights holder and object to a
    specific quotation, write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and we will address it.
  </p>

  <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
  <p>
    Factual errors: <a href="/about/corrections/">corrections policy</a>. Anything else:
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}> {SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
